## System information\n\nwindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen HTTPRequest uses threads, a physical network disconnection causes a permanent deadlock.\nThe worker thread gets stuck in a blocking socket call, so when cancel_request() (called manually or via queue_free()) triggers wait_to_finish(), the main thread hangs indefinitely.\nEven if a timeout is set, it is ignored or fails to resolve the freeze because the cleanup process itself is blocked.\nA mechanism is needed to force-break the socket block or allow non-blocking cancellation.\n\n\n### Tried Fixes (Not Working)\n\nI attempted the following modifications in void HTTPRequest::cancel_request(), but the issue persists:\n\n1. Calling client->close() before wait_to_finish(): This was intended to break the socket block, but it did not prevent the hang or caused crashes.\n\n2. Setting thread_request_quit without calling wait_to_finish(): While this avoids the immediate hang on the main thread, it leads to a crash when queue_free() is called because the Thread object is destroyed while the worker thread is still active.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Call `get_http_client_status()`, `get_downloaded_bytes()`, and `get_body_size()` every frame in the main thread while downloading a 120MB file in worker thread.\n2. Physically disconnect the LAN cable during the download.\n3. The application immediately enter freeze state.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"imdongye","id":42573050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTczMDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42573050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imdongye","html_url":"https://github.com/imdongye","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imdongye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imdongye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imdongye/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imdongye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subsc